<spell-notebook "markdown theming">
	<header level="1">
		Markdown
		<header>Markdown renders GitHub-flavoured markdown -- tables, task lists, code blocks -- from the element's
              own text or a file on this site.</>
	</>
	<markdown-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-markdown-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for all
			markdown), or on the rendered `<article>` through `::part(body)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the
			sheet reads each through a private alias. Never set the `--_ui-markdown-*` names: they're the sheet's private
			plumbing.

			Code blocks are `<ui-code>` elements, so the `--ui-code-*` tokens colour them (see Code's Theming tab).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every block of markdown on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-markdown-link-color: var(--ui-teal);
			  --ui-markdown-line-height: 1.6;
			}
			/* a quieter README */
			ui-markdown.readme {
			  --ui-markdown-heading-color: var(--ui-grey);
			}
			/* serif headings, no rule under them, a hairline `hr` */
			ui-markdown.guide {
			  --ui-markdown-heading-font-family: var(--ui-font-family-heading);
			  --ui-markdown-heading-weight: 700;
			  --ui-markdown-heading-rule: none;
			  --ui-markdown-heading-rule-gap: 0;
			  --ui-markdown-hr-height: 1px;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-markdown" playground>
				<ui-markdown source="/components/ui/examples/readme.md" heading-offset="4"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Markdown is ours, not Fomantic's:  the theme menu in the header changes the page around it.  Its
			colours follow the light or dark scheme.  The Spell theme (`spell`) gives it the brand's Design
			Guide look:  bold serif headings without a rule, a hairline `hr`, bold text and inline code in the
			strong ink.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
